---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import LegalContent from '../../components/LegalContent.astro';
import { EMAIL } from '../../lib/contact';
import { useTranslations } from '../../i18n/utils';

const lang = Astro.currentLocale ?? 'pt';
const t = useTranslations(lang);
---

<Layout
  title={`${t('legal.termosTitle')} — Astromidnight`}
  description={t('legal.termosMetaDesc')}
>
  <Header />
  <main class="pt-28 pb-24 sm:pt-32">
    <LegalContent title={t('legal.termosTitle')} updated={t('legal.updatedDate')}>
      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Astromidnight is the astrophotography and stargazing activity of David Cruz,
        carried out as a sole trader from a private observatory in São Pedro da
        Gafanhoeira, Alentejo, Portugal (Tax ID: 205254128). These terms apply
        to the website astromidnight.pt and to all services and products booked or
        purchased through it.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Services</h2>
      <p>We provide the following services, always at the observatory or another agreed location:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Stargazing, individual or in groups;</li>
        <li>Portraits Under the Stars;</li>
        <li>Astrophotography sessions and deep-sky image-editing mentorship;</li>
        <li>Stargazing sessions for groups and guests of rural stays;</li>
        <li>Sale of photographic prints in the site's shop.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Bookings and payment</h2>
      <p>
        Session and workshop bookings are made through our booking engine
        (Cal.com/Cal.eu), embedded in the site or opened directly. Payment is
        processed at that point, through the method shown in the booking form
        itself. Prices shown on the site are in euros and may change without notice
        for future bookings — the price that applies is always the one confirmed at
        the time of booking.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Cancellation, rescheduling and bad weather</h2>
      <p>
        If weather conditions don't allow a stargazing, portrait or astrophotography
        session to go ahead, you always have the option to reschedule for another
        night or receive a full refund — you never lose what you paid because of
        clouds. You can also ask to reschedule for other reasons by contacting us
        with reasonable notice; rescheduling outside the bad-weather policy is
        assessed case by case.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Print shop</h2>
      <p>
        Each print is made to order after purchase, with a preparation time of up to
        3 business days, followed by shipping (2 to 5 business days for Europe, up
        to 7 business days for the US and Canada, and up to 14 business days for
        other destinations). Payment is processed by the external checkout platform
        shown on each product — we do not store payment card data on our systems.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Taking part in stargazing sessions</h2>
      <p>
        Sessions take place outdoors, at night, on rural terrain. Participants
        should dress appropriately for the night-time cold and follow the
        instructions given on site, particularly regarding the handling of
        equipment. Minors must always be accompanied by a responsible adult.
        Participation is at each person's own risk, within what is reasonable given
        the nature of the activity.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The photographs, text and other content published on the site are the
        property of David Cruz, unless stated otherwise. They may not be copied,
        redistributed or used commercially without prior written permission —
        including photographs delivered in portrait sessions, whose personal-use
        terms are agreed at the time of delivery.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Complaints</h2>
      <p>
        If you have a complaint, contact us directly — we resolve things far faster
        than any outside body. This business also has an Electronic Complaints Book
        (Livro de Reclamações Eletrónico), available at <a href="https://www.livroreclamacoes.pt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">livroreclamacoes.pt</a>.
        In the event of an unresolved consumer dispute, you can turn to an
        alternative dispute resolution body — see the list at <a href="https://www.consumidor.gov.pt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">consumidor.gov.pt</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms periodically. The version in force is always the
        one published on this page, with the update date shown at the top.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Applicable law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by Portuguese law. For any dispute not resolved out
        of court, the court of the consumer's place of residence has jurisdiction,
        under applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For any question about these terms, write to <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </LegalContent>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
